        "Charles L. Bennett",
        "David N. Spergel",
        "Lyman A. Page Jr."
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "WMAP precision mapping converted the cosmic microwave background into a quantitatively powerful probe of cosmology.",
        "attribution": "Bennett and Page led the measurement effort, and Spergel was central to extracting its cosmological implications.",
        "maturity": "The measurements were highly controlled, broadly confirmed, and remain a benchmark for precision cosmology.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The boundary of credit relative to prior COBE recognition and later Planck measurements requires review."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 7,
